From: Harris Hancock <harris@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:31:26 +0100
Subject: Build V8 release archives without metagen

workerd builds V8 from GitHub source archives, which do not include the
llvm-libclang and llvm-build dependencies downloaded by gclient. V8's
metagen instance-type generator needs them, so the archive cannot be
built with it.

V8 15.6 enables metagen by default. Default
v8_use_metagen_instance_types to False so V8 uses the Torque-emitted
instance types, as it did by default before 15.6.

V8 also requires the optional metagen Clang header glob to match while
loading the Bazel package, even when metagen is disabled. Allow the glob
to be empty. Builds that enable metagen still require the actual Clang
headers.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index 74bc831191fc833939bc4429b093b7e2ce5404a6..55d5150ef335d04f4bca0c9f9606c95651102477 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -192,9 +192,13 @@ v8_flag(name = "v8_enable_experimental_tq_to_tsa")
 # Mirrors the GN arg of the same name: selects which instance-type
 # generator's output V8 compiles in, metagen or Torque's emission. When
 # off, the metagen action is not part of the build graph.
+#
+# Off by default for workerd: the harvest needs the llvm-libclang and
+# llvm-build gclient dependencies, which are not in the V8 source
+# tarball that the workerd build fetches.
 v8_flag(
     name = "v8_use_metagen_instance_types",
-    default = True,
+    default = False,
 )
 
 v8_flag(
@@ -4593,7 +4597,7 @@ filegroup(
     name = "metagen_clang_builtin_headers",
     srcs = glob([
         "third_party/llvm-build/Release+Asserts/lib/clang/*/include/**",
-    ]),
+    ], allow_empty = True),
 )
 
 # The harvest's checked-in C++ driver, shared with GN and metagen.py. It
